{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>If a corpse is found.</b> After it mentioned war against enemies, it mentions a person fighting with another." "<b>If a corpse is found.</b> And not hidden under a cairn." "<b>Fallen.</b> And not hanging on a tree, for it is not the way of a murderer to delay and hide and hang, because he fears for his life. Another interpretation: <b>fallen</b> — lying, for one cannot say that he fell when he saw him, since he found him already slain. <b>In the field</b> — and not floating on the face of the water, for it is impossible to distinguish where he came from."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:31.159765486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}